    "locked": false,
    "title": "Retire RC4 cipher support in SSH",
    "user": {
      "login": "jpantonow",
      "id": 129221613,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOB7PD7Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129221613?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/jpantonow",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpantonow/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "`BaseRC4Cipher.init` currently initializes RC4 with the supplied key, and `SshBuilder.setUpDefaultCiphers` offers Arcfour variants by default. RVSec reported that the `SecretKeySpec` call uses `ARCFOUR`, which its rule rejects. RFC 8758 prohibits Arcfour and RC4 in SSH, including the RFC 4345 variants.\n\nI changed initialization to clear the existing cipher and throw, and removed the Arcfour factories from the defaults while retaining the other ciphers and their availability checks. This also removes the reported `Cipher` transformation violation in `init`. Peers that support only RC4 will no longer negotiate with the default configuration.\n\nI chose to retire RC4 support rather than retain interoperability with peers that require it.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
